🚀 Day 16 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 18 – 4Sum.

This problem extended the concepts I learned in 3Sum and helped me understand how to efficiently find unique quadruplets using Sorting + Nested Loops + Two Pointers while carefully handling duplicates and integer overflow.

💡 Approach: Sorting + Two Pointers

I first sorted the array. Then:

Fixed the first element (i), skipping duplicates.
Fixed the second element (j), again skipping duplicates.
Used two pointers (left and right) to search for the remaining two elements.
Compared the current sum with the target:
If the sum was smaller, I moved the left pointer.
If the sum was greater, I moved the right pointer.
If the sum matched the target, I stored the quadruplet and skipped duplicate values to ensure unique results.

I also used long long while calculating the sum to safely handle integer overflow for large input values.

This optimized the brute-force O(n⁴) solution to O(n³).

📚 What I Learned:
✅ Extending the 3Sum pattern to solve 4Sum
✅ Combining Sorting + Two Pointers for optimization
✅ Handling duplicate elements to avoid repeated quadruplets
✅ Preventing integer overflow using long long
✅ Reducing time complexity from O(n⁴) to O(n³)

